```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: Operators of multi-step LLM agents (coding, tool-use, web-automation) who want to abort doomed trajectories early to save compute/cost, but only if their stack is limited to naive verbalized self-confidence (AUROC ~0.5-0.70) and cannot deploy online stepwise self-evaluation. The packet shows the monitor only wins in that weak-confidence regime; when confidence is extracted via stepwise self-evaluation (the regime prior art already occupies), the monitor loses.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only vs a naive baseline. EXP-0033: monitor AUC 0.743 loses to self-confidence AUC 0.749 (d=-0.006, 95% CI [-0.011,-0.001]) and flags only 42% of failures ≥1 step early (< pre-reg 0.5 bar). EXP-0034 flip-point at sigma_conf≈0.50 (confidence AUC≈0.696) is within verbalized-confidence miscalibration (arXiv 2602.06948, 2601.07264, 2502.11028), but published online stepwise self-evaluators operate at AUC~0.9 (Mavi et al. 2511.07364) and AUROC 0.94 (Vasudev et al. 2602.03338) — far below the flip, where the packet's own model says the monitor loses. The one robust win (+0.095 vs static difficulty, CI [+0.087,+0.103]) is the least-novel half and is implicit in PRM step-scoring (Lightman 2023) and AgentBoard progress-rate (Ma NeurIPS24).
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Prior art already deploys online stepwise failure detection at ~0.9 AUC, dominating the monitor's 0.743; Lead-time coverage 42% is insufficient for reliable early-abort, guaranteeing false negatives; The "distinct from difficulty" signal is already captured by PRMs and progress-rate metrics, offering no differentiation; Instrumentation overhead (tool-error/retry, looping, info-gain) for a signal that loses to the agent's own stepwise self-evaluation; The monitor only beats naive verbalized confidence, a baseline that production agent stacks are already moving away from via online LLM-as-Judge patterns]
RATIONALE: EXP-0033 global_summary.csv: monitor AUC 0.743 vs confidence 0.749 (d=-0.006, CI [-0.011,-0.001]); lead-time ≥1 step coverage 42.4% < 0.5 bar; vs difficulty d=+0.095 CI [+0.087,+0.103]. EXP-0034 sweep_sigma_conf.csv: flip at sigma_conf 0.50 (confidence AUC 0.696); monitor independent at 0.7427. Prior-art live check: Mavi et al. 2511.07364 "Self-Evaluating LLMs for Multi-Step Tasks" reports stepwise failure-detection AUC-ROC ~0.9 (online-capable); Vasudev et al. 2602.03338 reports LLM critic AUROC 0.94. The packet's synthesis concludes the space is occupied and the lead-time novelty is unsupported (42% < 0.5). The negative result is actionable: do not spend GPU L1; the cheap L0 correctly avoided waste by showing the monitor is relabeling of online stepwise failure detection with an unsupported lead-time framing.
```
